265
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,760
K. Yes, sir.

266
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:32,280
A. And her shock that she could so betray

267
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:37,480
this relationship that she'd had in doing her exercise,

268
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:42,920
in just a couple of words, was almost...

269
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:43,399
K. Very revealing.

270
00:18:43,399 --> 00:18:46,360
A. Yes, extremely revealing, but at the same time

271
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,320
desperately hard to believe

272
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:51,320
that anybody would do such a thing to himself.

273
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,360
Please, please, go on.

274
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:56,120
K. Sir, sir, that's it.

275
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,560
Negation can only take place

276
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:02,120
when the mind sees the false.

277
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:05,640
The very perception of the false

278
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:08,600
is the negation of the false.

279
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:13,000
And when you see the religions,

280
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:17,800
based on miracles, based on personal worship,

281
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:22,840
based on the fear that you, yourself, your own life

282
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:28,680
is so shoddy, empty, meaningless, and it is so transient,

283
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:33,960
so distant, you're gone in a few years,

284
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:37,960
and the mind creates the image which is eternal,

285
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:44,600
which is marvellous, which is the beautiful, the heaven,

286
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:48,520
and identifies with it and worships it.

287
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:56,440
Because it needs a sense of security, deeply,

288
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:03,400
and it has created all this superficial nonsense,

289
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,560
a circus, it is a circus.

290
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:06,440
A. Oh, yes.

291
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:13,000
K. So, can the mind observe this phenomenon

292
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:19,280
and see its own demand

293
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:25,080
for security, comfort, safety, permanency,

294
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,680
and deny all that?

295
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,960
Deny in the sense, see how the brain, thought,

296
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,000
creates the sense of permanency,

297
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,360
eternity, or whatever you like to call it,

298
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,400
and to see all that.

299
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:52,200
Therefore, one has to go much more deeply, I think,

300
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,200
into the question of thought.

301
00:20:56,600 --> 00:21:00,600
Because both in the West and the East,

302
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:06,520
thought has become the most important movement in life.

303
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:09,320
Right, sir? A. Oh, yes.

304
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:12,479
K. Thought, which has created

305
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:15,639
this marvellous world of technology,

306
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:20,040
marvellous world of science and all that,

307
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:23,560
and thought which has created the religions,

308
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:31,639
all the marvellous chants,

309
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:34,680
both the Gregorian and the Sanskrit chants,

310
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:40,600
thought which has built these beautiful cathedrals,

311
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:47,640
thought which has made images of the saviours,

312
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:52,600
the masters, the gurus, the father image,

313
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,800
and lest one, for example,

314
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:02,600
unless one really understands thought,

315
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:05,320
what is thinking,

316
00:22:07,639 --> 00:22:09,839
we will still play the

317
00:22:09,839 --> 00:22:12,040
same game in a different field.

318
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:15,560
A. Exactly.

319
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:18,360
K. Look what is happening in this country.

320
00:22:19,879 --> 00:22:23,879
These gurus come from India.

321
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:26,440
These gurus come from India.

322
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:31,480
They shave their head, put on the Indian dress,

323
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,440
a little tuft of hair hanging down,

324
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:39,160
and repeat endlessly what somebody has said.

325
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:44,360
A new guru. They have had old gurus, the priests,

326
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:47,720
the Catholic, and they have denied them,

327
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:51,320
but accept the others. You follow?

328
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:51,880
A. Yes.

329
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:55,080
K. The others are as dead as the old ones,

330
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,280
because they are just repeating tradition,

331
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:03,080
traditionally repeating how to sit, how to shave,

332
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:05,640
how to meditate, how to hold your head, breathe,

333
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:10,680
and finally obey what the old guru says,

334
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:12,040
or the young guru says,

335
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:18,440
which is exactly what took place in the Catholic world,

336
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,720
in the Protestant world. You follow?

337
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:22,360
They deny that, and yet accept the other,

338
00:23:24,200 --> 00:23:26,680
because they want security.

339
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:29,520
They want somebody to tell them

340
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:31,320
what to do, what to think.

341
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,440
Never how to think.

342
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:39,960
A. No. This raises a question

343
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:43,640
that I hope we can explore together,

344
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:46,520
that concerns the word experience.

345
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:48,280
K. Oh yes, that's another one.

346
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:54,520
It's amazing how often, in these times,

347
00:23:55,639 --> 00:24:00,280
this word crops up to represent something

348
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:06,920
that I desperately need, which somehow lies outside myself.

349
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:12,200
I need the experience of an awakening.

350
00:24:13,639 --> 00:24:16,120
It isn't an awakening that I need, apparently,

351
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:19,320
it's an experience of this awakening.

352
00:24:21,639 --> 00:24:26,840
The whole idea of religion as experience

353
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:30,840
seems to me to need very, very careful thought,

354
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:32,840
very, very careful penetration.

355
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:33,719
K. Quite true.

356
00:24:33,719 --> 00:24:34,520
A. Very careful penetration.

357
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:37,320
K. Sir, if I may

358
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:40,120
ask, why do we demand experience?

359
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,719
Why do we demand ourselves?

360
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:47,320
Why is this craving for experience?

361
00:24:53,639 --> 00:24:56,040
We have sexual experience,

362
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:59,399
experiences of every kind, don't we?

363
00:24:59,399 --> 00:25:00,439
As we live.

364
00:25:02,760 --> 00:25:08,840
Insults, flattery, happenings, incidents, influences,

365
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:10,800
people say, don't say, will you read

366
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,760
a book, and so on, so on.

367
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:15,159
We are experiencing all the time.

368
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:17,959
We are bored with that.

369
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:23,000
And we say, we go to somebody

370
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:26,040
who will give me the experience of God.

371
00:25:28,199 --> 00:25:30,600
A. Yes, that's precisely what's claimed.

372
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:35,560
K. Yes. Now, what is involved in that?

373
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:45,639
What is involved in the demand for experience

374
00:25:45,639 --> 00:25:50,439
and the experiencing of that demand?

375
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:58,040
I experience what that guru

376
00:25:58,040 --> 00:26:01,000
or master or somebody tells me.

377
00:26:01,480 --> 00:26:04,600
How do I know it is real?

378
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:09,240
And I recognise it, don't I, sir?

379
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,959
Look, I experience something.

380
00:26:15,159 --> 00:26:19,560
And I can only know that I have experienced it

381
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:22,280
only when I have recognised it.

382
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:25,240
Right?

383
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,040
A. Right.

384
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:30,840
K. Recognition implies I've already known.

385
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,040
A. Recognise.

386
00:26:32,040 --> 00:26:33,080
K. Recognise.

387
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:33,959
A. Yes.

388
00:26:33,959 --> 00:26:40,120
K. So, I am experiencing what I have already known,

389
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,760
therefore it's nothing new.

390
00:26:44,919 --> 00:26:47,800
A. Yes, you are making yourself very, very clear.

391
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:52,439
K. So, all they are doing is a self-deception.

392
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:55,720
A. It is actually lusted after.

393
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,560
K. Oh, good Lord!

394
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:01,240
A. Yes. The drive for it is extraordinary.

395
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:03,640
I've seen it in many, many students

396
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:06,920
who will go to extraordinary austerities.

397
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:07,880
Really.

398
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:08,920
K. Oh, I've noticed.

399
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:12,840
A. We sometimes think that young people today

400
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:15,080
are very loose in their behavior.

401
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:15,880
K. Yes.

402
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:17,720
A. But I have seen it.

403
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:20,440
We sometimes think that young people today

404
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:22,920
are very loose in their behavior.

405
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:27,240
Well, some are, but what's so new about that?

406
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:29,400
That's been going on since time out of mind.

407
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:32,360
I think that what is rarely seen

408
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:36,600
is that many, many young persons today

409
00:27:36,600 --> 00:27:42,120
are extremely serious about acquiring something

410
00:27:42,120 --> 00:27:45,320
that someone possesses that they don't have.

411
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:47,400
And if someone claims to have it,

412
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:49,560
naively, they are on their way.

413
00:27:49,560 --> 00:27:52,920
And they'll go through any number of cartwheels,

414
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:55,240
they'll stand on their head indefinitely

415
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:56,920
for that that lies out.

416
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,040
K. I have seen all this.

417
00:27:58,040 --> 00:28:02,440
A. Yes, which is called an experience as such.

418
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:05,720
K. That's why one has to be very careful,

419
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:10,360
as you pointed out, sir, to explore this word

420
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:15,000
and to see why the mind,

421
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:19,240
why a human being demands more experience.

422
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:24,360
When his whole life is a vast experience

423
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:27,000
with which he is so bored,

424
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:31,320
he thinks this is a new experience.

425
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:37,000
But to experience the new,

426
00:28:38,840 --> 00:28:41,880
how can the mind recognise it as the new?

427
00:28:42,840 --> 00:28:45,240
And this has already known it.

428
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:46,680
I don't know if I...

429
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:47,400
A. Yes, yes.

430
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:49,480
And there's something very remarkable here

431
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:51,480
in terms of what you said earlier.

432
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:54,760
In other previous conversations that we've had,

433
00:28:55,560 --> 00:29:00,040
in the recognition of what is called the new,

434
00:29:01,720 --> 00:29:05,000
the linkage with old thought, old image,

435
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:09,160
establishes the notion that there's something gradual

436
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:10,680
in the transition,

437
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:14,920
that there really is some kind of genuine link here

438
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:17,720
with where I am now and where I was before.

439
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:22,120
Now I become the next guru who goes out

440
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:25,080
and teaches the person how gradually

441
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,680
to undertake this discipline.

442
00:29:26,680 --> 00:29:27,560
K. Yes, sir.

443
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,600
A. And it never stops.

444
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:31,800
No, no, no, I do see that.

445
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:33,480
It's amazing, it's amazing.

446
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:34,920
Driving down in the car this morning,

447
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:39,880
I was thinking about the whole business of chant.

448
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:43,400
That you mentioned, the beauty of it all.

449
00:29:44,280 --> 00:29:47,720
And since this is related to experience as such,

450
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:52,200
I thought maybe we could examine the aesthetics

451
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:59,480
in terms of where this self-trapping lies in it.

452
00:30:00,520 --> 00:30:03,080
And of course, I thought of Sanskrit

453
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:08,280
and that beautiful invocation that is chanted

454
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:11,399
to the Upanishad, the Isha.

455
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:19,160
Purnam adhar, purnam idam, purnat purnam udhacate,

456
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:24,200
purnasya purnam, and it goes on.

457
00:30:27,080 --> 00:30:28,600
And I said to myself,

458
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:34,120
if one would attend to those words,

459
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:38,520
there's the echo of the abiding through the whole thing,

460
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,439
through that whole glorious cadence.

461
00:30:40,439 --> 00:30:45,159
And yet within it, within it, there's

462
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:52,679
the radical occasion to fall into a euphoria.

463
00:30:52,679 --> 00:30:53,639
K. Yes, sir.

464
00:30:53,639 --> 00:30:56,360
A. And somnolence takes over.

465
00:30:57,159 --> 00:30:59,080
But it's within the very same.

466
00:30:59,080 --> 00:31:01,080
And I said to myself, well,

467
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:05,480
maybe Mr. Krishnamurti would say a word about the relation

468
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:09,480
of beauty to this in terms

469
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:12,600
of one's own relation to the beautiful,

470
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:17,080
when that relation is not seen for what it is.

471
00:31:17,560 --> 00:31:21,720
Since there's an archosis present that I can generate,

472
00:31:22,439 --> 00:31:24,280
it isn't in those words.

473
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,600
And yet we think that

474
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:28,600
the language must be at fault.

475
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:32,520
There must be something demonically hypnotic about this.

476
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:33,320
We do.

477
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:35,920
And then religious groups will

478
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,520
separate themselves totally from all this.

479
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:41,079
We had a period in

480
00:31:41,079 --> 00:31:43,639
Europe when Protestants, Calvinists wouldn't allow

481
00:31:43,639 --> 00:31:46,520
the use of the word, the word, to be used.

482
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,480
And we had a period in Europe

483
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,440
when we had a period in Europe

484
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:55,480
when Protestants, Calvinists wouldn't allow an organ to...

485
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,120
No music.

486
00:31:56,120 --> 00:31:56,760
K. No music.

487
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:58,200
A. Because music is seductive.

488
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:02,040
I'm not the self-seducer, it's the music's fault.

489
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:02,760
K. Yes.

490
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:03,960
A. Let's look at that.

491
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:04,760
K. That is just it.

492
00:32:10,360 --> 00:32:14,280
As we were saying the other day, sir, beauty

493
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:17,079
can only be when there is

494
00:32:17,079 --> 00:32:19,879
the total abandonment of the self,

495
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:25,880
complete emptying the consciousness of

496
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:29,160
its content, which is the me.

497
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:35,240
Then there is a beauty which is something entirely different

498
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,800
from the pictures, charms, all that.

499
00:32:38,360 --> 00:32:41,280
And probably most of these young

500
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:44,200
people, and also the older people,

501
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:47,559
seek beauty in that sense

502
00:32:47,559 --> 00:32:50,919
through the trappings of the church,

503
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:55,880
through charms, through reading the

504
00:32:55,880 --> 00:33:00,040
Old Testament with all its...

505
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:03,159
beautiful words and images and all that,

506
00:33:03,159 --> 00:33:09,159
and that gives them a sense of deep satisfaction.

507
00:33:10,760 --> 00:33:13,480
In other words, sir, what

508
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:16,200
they are seeking is really gratification

509
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,399
through beauty.

510
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:23,560
Beauty of word, beauty of things, beauty of the word,

511
00:33:23,560 --> 00:33:25,479
beauty of the word, beauty of

512
00:33:25,479 --> 00:33:27,399
the word, beauty of the word.

513
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:31,000
Beauty of word, beauty of

514
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,640
charm, beauty of all the robes

515
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:37,400
and the incense and the light of the...

516
00:33:40,280 --> 00:33:44,600
coming through those marvellous pieces of colour.

517
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:46,840
You've seen it all in cathedrals,

518
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:50,040
North Qadam and Shaq and all these pieces.

519
00:33:50,040 --> 00:33:50,840
More.

520
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:55,720
And it gives them a sense of sacredness,

521
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:59,560
a sense of feeling happy, relieved.

522
00:34:00,840 --> 00:34:03,080
At last there is a place

523
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:05,320
where I can go and meditate,

524
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:09,800
be quiet, get into contact with something.

525
00:34:12,679 --> 00:34:14,119
And when you come along

526
00:34:14,119 --> 00:34:15,560
and say, look, that's all rubbish.

527
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:18,760
It has no meaning.

528
00:34:19,239 --> 00:34:20,679
What has meaning is how

529
00:34:20,679 --> 00:34:22,120
you live in your daily life.

530
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:25,239
Then they throw a brick at you.

531
00:34:25,239 --> 00:34:26,639
A. Of course, it's like taking

532
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:28,040
food away from a starving dog.

533
00:34:28,040 --> 00:34:29,239
K. Exactly.

534
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:35,080
